Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||05-22-2001||02:35 AM||||been talking to a friend aff forum, and we were discussing the merits of both the 3.4 and the caddy, and the 4.9 came out on top - the torque sounds fun! with the relatively low horsepower rating, we were a mite concerned, but began discussing turbocharging the 4.9, and were wondering what this would take (engine parts wise, and computer wise) were thinking of like 7 punds of boost from the turdocharger, should that be safe, and would it make significant gains?||||reg||1
Z||000001||KRMFiero||05-22-2001||07:07 AM||||Hmmm i would love to know what would work on my 4.5, I asked Joe a few months back, he reccomended the turbo and everything out of a Grand National, i have never seen one in a junk yard though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I was wondering if say twin turbo's off like a 2.3 T-Bird would work or something?  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||05-22-2001||09:27 AM||||what about one from a 301 trans am turbo? the engine size would be similar. <P>i've also seen an article in muscle mustangs and fast fords mag (apr.'98) where they used 2 t-bird turbos on a 5 litre mustang. they do it for $1000 with junkyard parts (and i'm sure agreat deal more know how than i could throw at it to keep it that inexpensive).  don't know how much could be applied to this idea though. be interesting.||||reg||1
