Z||000004||FieroSTETZ||05-22-2001||12:42 PM||||well, i think i could find one off a diesel truck pretty easy - i have an old issue of (i think it was hot rod?) a magazine showing how to rebuild a diesel turbo for gasoline use - might look into that, and apparently the rebuild kits are like 50 bucks - i want to know about the computer side of it though... are there aftermarket computers that could work?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1012904&a=7460757&p=25516673&Sequence=0&res=high"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||BV MotorSports||05-22-2001||03:10 PM||||Contact me off-line and I can help you plan out a nice turbo set-up.<BR>2.3 t-bird turbo = too small<BR>for the 4.9 v8 you need a turbo w/ a CFM rating of 600cfm or larger. <BR>A 16 or 20g mitubishi turbo<BR>Garret t3 or t4 (sweet turbo)<BR>since this is a "v" engine you will need a custom made stainless steel crossover pipe made with the correct mounting flange for the turbo you choose.<BR>A MSD BTM for ignition <BR>oil, coolant and return lines need fabricated as well as heat shields and down pipe.<BR>Alot of the info on Dennis' homemade turbo set up page will help you out a great deal.<BR>Since I am into turbo charged cars....I should be able to help you out. <BR>BTW try to find a Conquest/Starion intercooler...Very efficient and fairly common. Dont even bother to turbo w/o using an intercooler w/ over 6psi of boost.<P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
